IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sazwt-law`

-- Seat layer: a soldier serving within the remit of the Federal Ministry of Defence, not posted to an establishment in the annex to SAZV § 1(2),
-- not engaged in an activity listed in SG § 30c(4), and below pay grade B 6 (so SAZV § 19 does not lift the weekly working-time rules).
-- Those four are assumptions of the seat, not inputs (NOTES.md, Seat).
-- It asks that soldier's questions under both readings, takes plain facts as inputs, builds the law layer's records internally and calls the law layer.
-- It restates no rule. Target compiler: main.
-- A record field that a question does not read gets a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so.

GIVEN `reduction`       IS A NUMBER
      `departure`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `against`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The soldier's working week`
`the working week of a soldier with` MEANS
    `The soldier's working week` WITH
        `percent by which part-time employment reduces the working time` IS `reduction`
        `service reasons call for a departure from Monday to Friday` IS `departure`
        `service reasons stand against the individual distribution applied for` IS `against`

GIVEN `hours`           IS A NUMBER
      `reasons`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `area`            IS AN `Area of service`
      `happened`        IS A `What has happened`
      `workload`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `continuity`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The soldier's working day`
`the working day of a soldier with` MEANS
    `The soldier's working day` WITH
        `hours of regular daily working time fixed for the day, breaks included` IS `hours`
        `service reasons require more than 13 hours` IS `reasons`
        `the area of service` IS `area`
        `what has happened` IS `happened`
        `it leads to an excessive workload that could not be foreseen` IS `workload`
        `the continuity of the service must be ensured in the activity` IS `continuity`

GIVEN `on call`         IS A NUMBER
      `called on`       IS A NUMBER
      `blocked`         IS A NUMBER
      `arrangement`     IS A `Working-time arrangement`
GIVETH A `The soldier's calendar month`
`the calendar month of a soldier with` MEANS
    `The soldier's calendar month` WITH
        `hours of Rufbereitschaft outside working time` IS `on call`
        `hours of it during which the soldier was actually called on` IS `called on`
        `hours of the compensation that compelling service reasons stand against` IS `blocked`
        `working-time arrangement` IS `arrangement`

§ `Over which days of the week may my regular weekly working time be distributed? (SAZV § 5(2))`

@export Over which days of the week may my regular weekly working time be distributed, under § 5(2) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation as printed (amended in 2025)? Answers Monday to Friday, Monday to Saturday or any days of the week.
GIVEN
    `part-time reduction in percent`             IS A NUMBER  @desc By how many percent your working time is reduced because you work part time; 0 if you work full time.
    `service reasons call for other days`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if your superiors say that service reasons call for distributing your weekly hours other than over Monday to Friday.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Days the weekly working time may be distributed over`
`over which days may my weekly working time be distributed as printed` MEANS
    `the days the regular weekly working time may be distributed over under the reading` `as printed` (`the working week of a soldier with` `part-time reduction in percent` `service reasons call for other days` FALSE)  -- FALSE: placeholder, this question does not read the field

@export Over which days of the week may my regular weekly working time be distributed, if the 2025 amendment of § 5(2) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation is void because its preamble did not cite § 30c(5) sentence 1 no. 1 of the Soldiers Act? Answers Monday to Friday, Monday to Saturday, or nothing where the earlier text does not reach you.
GIVEN
    `part-time reduction in percent`             IS A NUMBER  @desc By how many percent your working time is reduced because you work part time; 0 if you work full time.
    `service reasons call for other days`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if your superiors say that service reasons call for distributing your weekly hours other than over Monday to Friday.
    `an exception applies`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether to assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2025 wording stands: false assumes none applies and the amendment is void.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Days the weekly working time may be distributed over`
`over which days may my weekly working time be distributed if the 2025 amendment is void` MEANS
    `the days the regular weekly working time may be distributed over under the reading` (`the reading to apply to the instruction` `Art. 5 No. 1: section 5(2)` `an exception applies`) (`the working week of a soldier with` `part-time reduction in percent` `service reasons call for other days` FALSE)  -- FALSE: placeholder, this question does not read the field

@export If I apply, may an individual distribution of my regular weekly working time over Monday to Friday be approved, under § 5(2) sentence 3 of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation as printed (inserted in 2025)? Answers yes or no.
GIVEN
    `service reasons stand against it`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if service reasons stand against the individual distribution over Monday to Friday you applied for.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`may an individual distribution be approved on my application as printed` MEANS
    `an individual distribution over Monday to Friday may be approved on application under the reading` `as printed` (`the working week of a soldier with` 0 FALSE `service reasons stand against it`)  -- 0 and FALSE: placeholders, this question does not read those fields

@export If I apply, may an individual distribution of my regular weekly working time over Monday to Friday be approved, if the 2025 amendment of § 5(2) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation is void? Answers yes or no, or nothing: the earlier text has no such sentence.
GIVEN
    `service reasons stand against it`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if service reasons stand against the individual distribution over Monday to Friday you applied for.
    `an exception applies`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether to assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2025 wording stands: false assumes none applies and the amendment is void.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`may an individual distribution be approved on my application if the 2025 amendment is void` MEANS
    `an individual distribution over Monday to Friday may be approved on application under the reading` (`the reading to apply to the instruction` `Art. 5 No. 1: section 5(2)` `an exception applies`) (`the working week of a soldier with` 0 FALSE `service reasons stand against it`)  -- 0 and FALSE: placeholders, this question does not read those fields

§ `May my regular daily working time today exceed 13 hours? (SAZV § 6(1))`

@export Is the regular daily working time fixed for me today allowed under § 6(1) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation as printed (sentence 3 recast in 2025), which limits it to 13 hours including breaks unless sentence 3 allows more? Answers yes or no.
GIVEN
    `hours fixed for today`                      IS A NUMBER  @desc The regular daily working time fixed for you today, in hours, breaks included.
    `service reasons require more than 13 hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if your superiors say that service reasons require a regular daily working time of more than 13 hours today.
    `area of service`                            IS AN `Area of service` @desc The area of your service today; another area if none of the listed ones.
    `what has happened`                          IS A `What has happened` @desc Whether an extraordinary event or an accident is behind today's work: nothing out of the ordinary, an extraordinary event, or an accident.
    `excessive unforeseeable workload`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if that event or accident leads to an excessive workload that could not be foreseen.
    `continuity must be ensured`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if your activity today is one in which the continuity of the service must be ensured.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is my daily working time today allowed as printed` MEANS
    `the regular daily working time fixed for the day is within section 6(1) under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` `hours fixed for today` `service reasons require more than 13 hours` `area of service` `what has happened` `excessive unforeseeable workload` `continuity must be ensured`)

@export Is the regular daily working time fixed for me today allowed under § 6(1) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation, if the 2025 recast of its sentence 3 is void, so that the earlier, illustrative list applies? Answers yes or no.
GIVEN
    `hours fixed for today`                      IS A NUMBER  @desc The regular daily working time fixed for you today, in hours, breaks included.
    `service reasons require more than 13 hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if your superiors say that service reasons require a regular daily working time of more than 13 hours today.
    `area of service`                            IS AN `Area of service` @desc The area of your service today; another area if none of the listed ones.
    `what has happened`                          IS A `What has happened` @desc Whether an extraordinary event or an accident is behind today's work: nothing out of the ordinary, an extraordinary event, or an accident.
    `excessive unforeseeable workload`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if that event or accident leads to an excessive workload that could not be foreseen.
    `continuity must be ensured`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if your activity today is one in which the continuity of the service must be ensured.
    `an exception applies`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether to assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2025 wording stands: false assumes none applies and the recast is void.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is my daily working time today allowed if the 2025 amendment is void` MEANS
    `the regular daily working time fixed for the day is within section 6(1) under the reading` (`the reading to apply to the instruction` `Art. 5 No. 3: section 6(1) sentence 3` `an exception applies`) (`the working day of a soldier with` `hours fixed for today` `service reasons require more than 13 hours` `area of service` `what has happened` `excessive unforeseeable workload` `continuity must be ensured`)

@export On which ground of § 6(1) sentence 3 of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation as printed (recast in 2025) may my regular daily working time today exceed 13 hours? Answers the first ground that applies, or that the 13-hour limit holds.
GIVEN
    `service reasons require more than 13 hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if your superiors say that service reasons require a regular daily working time of more than 13 hours today.
    `area of service`                            IS AN `Area of service` @desc The area of your service today; another area if none of the listed ones.
    `what has happened`                          IS A `What has happened` @desc Whether an extraordinary event or an accident is behind today's work: nothing out of the ordinary, an extraordinary event, or an accident.
    `excessive unforeseeable workload`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if that event or accident leads to an excessive workload that could not be foreseen.
    `continuity must be ensured`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if your activity today is one in which the continuity of the service must be ensured.
GIVETH A `Ground for exceeding 13 hours`
`on which ground may my daily working time today exceed 13 hours as printed` MEANS
    `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 0 `service reasons require more than 13 hours` `area of service` `what has happened` `excessive unforeseeable workload` `continuity must be ensured`)  -- 0: placeholder, the ground does not read the hours

@export On which ground of § 6(1) sentence 3 of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation may my regular daily working time today exceed 13 hours, if the 2025 recast of sentence 3 is void, so that the earlier, illustrative list applies? Answers the ground, or that the 13-hour limit holds.
GIVEN
    `service reasons require more than 13 hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if your superiors say that service reasons require a regular daily working time of more than 13 hours today.
    `area of service`                            IS AN `Area of service` @desc The area of your service today; another area if none of the listed ones.
    `what has happened`                          IS A `What has happened` @desc Whether an extraordinary event or an accident is behind today's work: nothing out of the ordinary, an extraordinary event, or an accident.
    `excessive unforeseeable workload`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if that event or accident leads to an excessive workload that could not be foreseen.
    `continuity must be ensured`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if your activity today is one in which the continuity of the service must be ensured.
    `an exception applies`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether to assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2025 wording stands: false assumes none applies and the recast is void.
GIVETH A `Ground for exceeding 13 hours`
`on which ground may my daily working time today exceed 13 hours if the 2025 amendment is void` MEANS
    `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` (`the reading to apply to the instruction` `Art. 5 No. 3: section 6(1) sentence 3` `an exception applies`) (`the working day of a soldier with` 0 `service reasons require more than 13 hours` `area of service` `what has happened` `excessive unforeseeable workload` `continuity must be ensured`)  -- 0: placeholder, the ground does not read the hours

-- This group only arises for a soldier who was on call (Rufbereitschaft) for more than 10 hours outside working time in the month.
-- A form can ask "Were you on call for more than 10 hours this month?" before showing it.
§ `How many hours of compensation am I owed for this month's on-call duty? (SAZV § 12)`

@export How many hours of compensation am I owed for this calendar month's on-call duty (Rufbereitschaft), under § 12 of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation as printed (amended in 2025 with effect from 1 January 2025)? Answers a number of hours, to be given within twelve months.
GIVEN
    `hours on call this month`                   IS A NUMBER  @desc The hours you were on call (Rufbereitschaft) outside your working time in this calendar month, from January 2025 on.
    `hours actually called on`                   IS A NUMBER  @desc Of those, the hours you were actually called on, from arriving at the place of duty to the end of the task; 0 if none.
    `hours compelling service reasons block`     IS A NUMBER  @desc The hours of that compensation that compelling service reasons stand against; 0 if none.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many hours of compensation am I owed for on-call duty as printed` MEANS
    `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `as printed` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` `hours on call this month` `hours actually called on` `hours compelling service reasons block` `fixed working time`)  -- fixed working time: placeholder, the number does not read the arrangement

@export How many hours of compensation am I owed for this calendar month's on-call duty (Rufbereitschaft), if the 2025 amendment of § 12(1) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation is void, so that compelling service reasons do not reduce it? Answers a number of hours, to be given within twelve months.
GIVEN
    `hours on call this month`                   IS A NUMBER  @desc The hours you were on call (Rufbereitschaft) outside your working time in this calendar month.
    `hours actually called on`                   IS A NUMBER  @desc Of those, the hours you were actually called on, from arriving at the place of duty to the end of the task; 0 if none.
    `hours compelling service reasons block`     IS A NUMBER  @desc The hours of that compensation that compelling service reasons stand against; 0 if none. Read only if an exception applies.
    `an exception applies`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether to assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2025 wording stands: false assumes none applies and the amendment is void.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`how many hours of compensation am I owed for on-call duty if the 2025 amendment is void` MEANS
    `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` (`the reading to apply to the instruction` `Art. 5 No. 4: section 12(1) sentence 2` `an exception applies`) (`the calendar month of a soldier with` `hours on call this month` `hours actually called on` `hours compelling service reasons block` `fixed working time`)  -- fixed working time: placeholder, the number does not read the arrangement

@export In what form is the compensation for my on-call duty given, under § 12(1) sentences 3 and 4 of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation (the same under both readings)? Answers time off, or a credit to the flexitime account.
GIVEN
    `working-time arrangement`                   IS A `Working-time arrangement` @desc Whether you work fixed working time or flexitime (Gleitzeit).
GIVETH A `Form of the compensation`
`in what form is the compensation for on-call duty given` MEANS
    `the form of the compensation` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 0 0 0 `working-time arrangement`)  -- 0, 0, 0: placeholders, the form does not read the hours

§ `Did the 2025 amending regulation cite the power these changes rest on?`

@export Does the preamble of the Regulation of 6 March 2025, which changed §§ 5(2), 6(1) and 12(1) of the Soldiers' Working Time Regulation, cite § 30c(5) sentence 1 no. 1 of the Soldiers Act (the power over regular working time) with § 93(2) no. 6? Answers yes or no, from the gazette text of the preamble.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`does the 2025 preamble cite the power over regular working time` MEANS
    `the preamble cites the power` (`the power the instruction rests on` `Art. 5 No. 3: section 6(1) sentence 3`) `the powers cited in the preamble of the 2025 amending regulation`

@export Does the preamble of the Regulation of 6 March 2025 name § 93(2) no. 6 of the Soldiers Act, the provision that makes the Ministry of Defence the maker of the regulation on regular working time under § 30c(5)? Answers yes or no, from the gazette text of the preamble.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`does the 2025 preamble name section 93(2) no. 6` MEANS
    `the preamble names section 93(2) no. 6 of the Soldiers Act` `the powers cited in the preamble of the 2025 amending regulation`
